{"name":"Greyhound","hex":"#b2aca2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Greyhound","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bus run by Greyhound Lines."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Greyhound"}],"entries":[{"title":"Greyhound","blocks":[{"text":"The Greyhound is a breed of dog and a sighthound. It is an ancient breed historically developed for hunting game by sight and speed, and has later been used in organised coursing and greyhound racing. Greyhounds are also kept as show dogs and companion animals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/GraceTheGreyhound.jpg/330px-GraceTheGreyhound.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greyhound","wikidata":"Q38571"},{"title":"Greyhound (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Greyhound is a 2020 American war film directed by Aaron Schneider and starring Tom Hanks, who also wrote the screenplay. The film is based on the 1955 novel The Good Shepherd by C. S. Forester, and follows a US Navy commander on his first assignment commanding a multi-national escort destroyer group of four, defending an Allied convoy from U-boats during the Battle of the Atlantic. The film also stars Stephen Graham, Rob Morgan, and Elisabeth Shue."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f3/Greyhound_poster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greyhound_(film)","wikidata":"Q50404285"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Blue_greyhound.JPG/500px-Blue_greyhound.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Blue_greyhound.JPG/1280px-Blue_greyhound.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Blue_greyhou